From 2404048bc5a1cfb66c1ccfa14e4a76b4d0bf8f87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vpestininkas <159783366+Vpestininkas@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:20:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] InputEventMonitor: read the privacy shutter switch bit,
 not bit 0

readRawValue() tested the configured switch with

    codeBits[code / 32] & (1UL << (code % 32)) != 0U

and != binds tighter than &, so this is codeBits[...] & 1: it reads
bit 0 of the word instead of the configured event code. For the
privacy shutter on SW_CAMERA_LENS_COVER (EV_SW code 9) that is
SW_LID's bit, which the reporting device does not have, so the initial
value is always 0. CameraDevice::start() treats 0 as "shutter closed"
and switches to the DummyImageSource, so the camera opens to a blank
frame every time, whatever the shutter state. Only a later switch event
moves it to the real sensor.

Seen on a Lenovo ThinkPad X9-15 Gen 1 (Lunar Lake, IMX471), whose
config sets privacyShutterEventType 5 / privacyShutterEventCode 9 and
whose thinkpad_acpi input device reports SW_CAMERA_LENS_COVER.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/core/InputEventMonitor.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/InputEventMonitor.cpp b/src/core/InputEventMonitor.cpp
index 7e51d17..7f6d68c 100644
--- a/src/core/InputEventMonitor.cpp
+++ b/src/core/InputEventMonitor.cpp
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@ int InputEventMonitor::readRawValue() {
     memset(codeBits, 0, sizeof(codeBits));
     status = ioctl(mFd, req, codeBits);
     if (status >= 0) {
-        mValue = (codeBits[mEventCode / U32_BITS] & (1UL << (mEventCode % U32_BITS)) != 0U) ? 1 : 0;
+        mValue = ((codeBits[mEventCode / U32_BITS] & (1UL << (mEventCode % U32_BITS))) != 0U) ? 1 : 0;
     }
 
     return status;
